  "id": "Compound::DB00705 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Delavirdine is linked to Cyp2c19 through a series of molecular interactions that involve both direct and indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Delavirdine, as a non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor, is included in a class of compounds that includes Etravirine, which in turn binds to Cyp2c19. This indicates a potential mechanism of action where Delavirdine may influence the activity of Cyp2c19 through its interaction with Etravirine, which is part of a broader metabolic pathway involving Cyp2c9. The presence of a lowest common ancestor in the class of non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors and the organonitrogen heterocyclic compound class further supports a shared biochemical profile. The integration of these pathways suggests that Delavirdine may modulate Cyp2c19 activity through a mechanism that involves the metabolic activation of substrates, possibly through the enzyme Cyp2c9. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link between Delavirdine and Cyp2c19, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
